+## Multi-row identity extension (revision 6)
+
+After the final `DWPR` program comes `DWPG`, a `u32 groupCount` and a
+`u32 geometryBytes`, followed by 24-byte group records and the geometry payload.
+Each record is:
+
+`u32 startProgramOffset, endProgramOffset, geometryOffset, firstProgramIndex;`
+`u16 createCount, rowDelta, nonemptySegments, reservedZero;`
+
+Program offsets are relative to the `DWPR` program payload, geometry offsets
+to the new geometry payload. `firstProgramIndex` includes the mirrored bit,
+as in `DWPR`. Records are sorted by start offset. A source-ordered cursor walks
+them once per selected pattern; the independent lookup remains a test oracle.
+
+Each geometry cell has two bytes: column/kind with the same encoding as the
+original Create stream, then an unsigned row offset relative to the group's
+first row, in units of 16 pixels. The second byte is **not** a draw count.
+Groups contain at least two nonempty segments, never cross a source event
+cell or pattern boundary, and do not include the optional repeated pillar tail.
+The loader verifies every coordinate and endpoint against the validated row
+programs before exposing a group.
+
+One admitted group creates one authoritative lifetime descriptor, retaining
+the geometry pointer for its lifetime. Publication mutations may split that
+descriptor; row-filtered consumers use each cell's row offset, not the group's
+origin. Room and layer clocks remain independent. Thin-platform retirement
+uses the extrema of platform rows only, with the same lifetime ceiling and
+revision changes as individual notifications.
+
+The backend may publish this ownership transaction before the source row
+programs only after proving that the whole group is allocation-free, has no
+intervening observers, and that row setters use an already-acquired borrowed
+position publication which cannot fail. RNG draws, occupancy, platform art,
+special-border counts and every builder row setter still execute in source
+order before the next event cell. Declined admission changes no ownership and
+falls back at the original row boundaries. No runtime geometry scratch array
+or per-row lifetime constructor is part of the grouped path.
+
 ## Portable reader
 
 `src/core/BuilderPatternPack` decodes each field byte-by-byte. Construction
